 :links [{:to "algebra-cubic" :relation :generalizes :note "Cardano's and Ferrari's formulas exist because the groups of the cubic and the quartic, S_3 and S_4, are solvable."}
         {:to "number-theory-gauss" :relation :generalizes :note "Gauss' periods of the 17-gon are the fixed fields of the subgroups of the cyclic group (Z/17)^*; Galois' Proposition I extends this to every equation."}
